From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:21:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Input: da7280 - support FF_RUMBLE

Desktop and phone userspace drives vibration motors through FF_RUMBLE
(feedbackd refuses a device without it: "No rumble capable vibra device";
hfd-service, used by Plasma Mobile, picks the first FF_RUMBLE device), but
the driver only offered FF_CONSTANT and FF_PERIODIC with custom waveforms,
so the input core's rumble emulation (a sine periodic effect) was rejected
with "Device can only accept FF_CUSTOM waveform".

Play a rumble effect like a constant one, at the stronger of the two
magnitudes (the Surface Duo has one motor), in the constant-effect
operating mode.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the
direction of Bryson, who tested it on his Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/input/misc/da7280.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/da7280.c b/drivers/input/misc/da7280.c
index e4a605c6a..ec2b26643 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/da7280.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/da7280.c
@@ -529,6 +529,21 @@ static int da7280_haptics_upload_effect(struct input_dev *dev,
 					0 : effect->u.constant.level;
 		break;
 
+	/*
+	 * A single motor: play the stronger of the two rumble magnitudes like a constant effect at that level
+	 * (userspace such as feedbackd only drives FF_RUMBLE devices).
+	 */
+	case FF_RUMBLE:
+		tmp = max(effect->u.rumble.strong_magnitude, effect->u.rumble.weak_magnitude);
+		haptics->op_mode = haptics->const_op_mode;
+		if (haptics->op_mode == DA7280_DRO_MODE) {
+			haptics->level = tmp * 254 / 0xFFFF;
+			break;
+		}
+
+		haptics->gain = tmp / 2;	/* 0..0xFFFF -> the constant effect's 0..0x7FFF */
+		break;
+
 	/* RTWM/ETWM modes support this type */
 	case FF_PERIODIC:
 		if (effect->u.periodic.waveform != FF_CUSTOM) {
@@ -1226,6 +1241,7 @@ static int da7280_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 
 	input_set_capability(haptics->input_dev, EV_FF, FF_PERIODIC);
 	input_set_capability(haptics->input_dev, EV_FF, FF_CUSTOM);
+	input_set_capability(haptics->input_dev, EV_FF, FF_RUMBLE);
 	input_set_capability(haptics->input_dev, EV_FF, FF_CONSTANT);
 	input_set_capability(haptics->input_dev, EV_FF, FF_GAIN);
 
